{"availability":"available","full":"krasninja/querycat","name":"querycat","description":"Use SQL to query different data sources like logs, JSON, CSV, XML, etc.","category":"Other","language":"C#","stars":25,"forks":3,"created":"2022-10-10T15:58:59Z","updated":"2026-10-15T06:55:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"develop","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://querycat.anti-soft.ru/playground/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:20.739Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:20.739Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T20:32:20.739Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:18.122Z","stars":24,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-10T23:18:50.438Z","stars":24,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-16T20:32:20.739Z","stars":25,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Query CSV, JSON, XML and log files with plain SQL - right from your terminal!","Installation | Examples | Tutorial | Documentation | Playground","QueryCat is a command line tool that lets you use SQL to query CSV, JSON, XML and log files - or the output of any other command. No need to import your data into Excel or a database first: point QueryCat at a file or pipe and query it as is."],"features":["Single binary, zero dependencies. Natively compiled - download it and run it.","Streaming pipeline. Rows are processed as they are read, so large files don't have to fit in memory.","Embeddable. Use it as a .NET library to query files or your own objects.","Inputs: CSV, TSV, JSON, XML, LTSV, IIS W3C, CLEF logs, plain text, stdin and more via plugins.","SQL: filtering, aggregates and GROUP BY, joins, ORDER BY, LIMIT/OFFSET, UNION, subqueries, CTEs (including recursive), window functions."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/krasninja/querycat/blob/develop/README.md","fingerprint":"d4c538619718bea27bdb1fa5346389d9a8503fb7a4611d403e3d0a5334b0b5b3","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T23:18:50.516Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T23:18:50.516Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"